<speech id="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2015-03-02a.204.2" speakerid="uk.org.publicwhip/member/40651" speakername="Rosie Cooper" colnum="204"  time="016:30:00" url="http://www.publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm201415/cmhansrd/cm150302/halltext/150302h0001.htm#150302h0001.htm_spnew11">
	<p pid="a.204.2/1">If the Government require dog owners to have dogs chipped, responsible dog owners have their dogs chipped. It is surely not beyond the wit of man or the Highways Agency to</p>
	<p pid="a.204.2/2">locate the owners of dogs without there being a great increase in work load or cost. It is ridiculous; are we really saying that this Government are now becoming one who do not care about pets and their loving owners? It is outrageous.</p>
</speech>
